I don't think that's a good idea.  You can easily price-ID out the
group of potions that contains polymorph and then work on identifying
the others.  Each price group generally only has one bad potion in it
that can be guarded against pretty easily (to guard against paralysis,
for instance, do it on top of an engraved Elbereth square behind a
locked door, or in a coaligned temple).  Potions are prime candidates
for IDing by using, and knowing which potions are which from as early
on as possible is definitely a survival advantage.


